'''Marovo''' is an [[Austronesian language]] of the [[Solomon Islands]]. It is spoken in the [[New Georgia Group]] on islands in [[Marovo Lagoon]] and on the neighbouring islands of [[New Georgia]], [[Vangunu]] and [[Nggatokae]]. The usual [[word order]] in sentences is [[Verb–subject–object word order|verb–subject–object]].

Names for local [[fauna]] are similar to but still much distinct from those in [[Roviana (language)|Roviana]] (and presumably other [[New Georgia languages]]).<ref>{{harvp|Read|Moseby|2006}}</ref>

